  "market_context": "EURUSD was in a recovery phase after a downtrend, with a bullish engulfing candle forming on the 1-hour chart around 1.09850–1.10000, prompting a long entry during London session.",
  "key_observation": "A bullish engulfing candle triggered a long entry with 20-pip stop; the analyst emphasized using two targets—first at 1:1 R:R to lock in half position profit, second at 4H resistance (1.10400) confirmed by multiple past rejections.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify a bullish engulfing candlestick pattern on the 1H chart as the entry trigger for a long position.",
    "Step 2: Place stop-loss 20 pips below the engulfing candle’s low.",
    "Step 3: Set first target at 1:1 risk-to-reward (20 pips) and close half the position upon reaching it to secure profit.",
    "Step 4: Zoom to the 4H chart to identify a major resistance level at 1.10400, validated by multiple prior rejections, and assign it as the second target.",
    "Step 5: Optionally move the stop-loss of the remaining half-position to break-even after the first target is hit."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Using multiple targets with partial profit-taking converts winning trades into guaranteed wins even if price reverses; aligning the second target with HTF structure increases probability of success.",
